{"t": 1794106463.6554263, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return page `number` (1-based) of `items`, with `size` items per page.\"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix pagination to use 1-based page numbers (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106466.5371685, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated `number` as a 0-based offset, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page even though the API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page).\n\nChanged the offset calculation to `(number - 1) * size`.\n\nVerification: `page(range(1, 11), 1, 3) == [1, 2, 3]`, `page(..., 2, 3) == [4, 5, 6]`, `page(..., 4, 3) == [10]`, out-of-range pages return `[]`.", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
